question:
A simple telescope has the following specifications: the objective lens has a focal length (F) of 24 cm and an aperture of 2 cm, while the eyepiece has a focal length (f) of 4 cm and an aperture of 1 cm.

Determine the following:
(a) the optimal position of the eye (modeled as a single point) to observe the maximum field of view of a distant object;
(b) the diameter of the exit pupil (eye ring);
(c) the maximum angular size of a fully visible object, assuming the eye is a point located at the eye position—solve this **both** by (i) using the telescope’s magnifying power, and (ii) without relying on magnifying power.

Select the correct set of answers from the provided options.

Compute the value of the convolution integral \( y(\tau) = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} x(\tau - t) v(t) \, dt \) at \(\tau = 2.5\) for the following rectangular signals:

\[ x(t) = \begin{cases}
1 & 0 \leq t \leq 3 \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}, \quad
v(t) = \begin{cases}
1 & 0 \leq t \leq 2 \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}. \]

Select the correct result from the provided options.
